---
title: "An image gallery"
---

Every figure is click-to-zoom, and a multi-image page becomes a navigable gallery:
open one and step through the rest with the ← / → arrow keys.

::: {layout-ncol=3}
![No pooling.](fit-b.png){#fig-no-pooling}

![Complete pooling.](fit-c.png){#fig-complete-pooling}

![Hierarchical (partial pooling).](fit-a.png){#fig-hierarchical}
:::

The three fits above (@fig-no-pooling, @fig-complete-pooling, and @fig-hierarchical)
zoom into one gallery: click any one, then step through the others with ← / →.

## Side-by-side columns

`::: {.columns}` with `.column` children (reveal.js muscle memory) is accepted as an alias
for `{layout-ncol}`, so a two-column split lays out side by side rather than silently stacking:

::: {.columns}
::: {.column}
The left column holds one idea.
:::

::: {.column}
The right column holds the other, beside it.
:::
:::
